  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tackling Antimicrobial Resistance in Colombia via diagnostic uptake in pig farming</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The aim of this project is to understand the potential of a novel subsidized diagnostic platform model to support increased diagnosis and appropriate antimicrobial use in the swine industry in Colombia, by identifying challenges and successes in its uptake. The project also aims to improve stakeholder engagement and knowledge transfer for more prudent use of antimicrobial (AMU) in Colombian pig farming.</narrative>
  </description>
